WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.545 --> 00:00:02.670
- He's an American motivational speaker,

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.496
author and minister.

00:00:04.496 --> 00:00:06.232
His speeches have been widely viewed

00:00:06.232 --> 00:00:07.860
and are popular on YouTube.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:11.221
Lebron James has credited him
as part of his inspiration

00:00:11.221 --> 00:00:14.618
for winning the 2012 MBA Championship.

00:00:14.618 --> 00:00:18.785
He's Eric Thomas and here are
his top ten rules for success.

00:00:21.628 --> 00:00:23.208
- You can't dangle somethin'
in front of my face.

00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:24.982
I don't want that.

00:00:24.982 --> 00:00:26.561
Many of you are taking anything

00:00:26.561 --> 00:00:27.968
'cause you don't know what you want.

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:30.422
If I can do one thing for
you when you leave this room,

00:00:30.422 --> 00:00:33.308
I don't want nothin' from you
but for you to leave this room

00:00:33.308 --> 00:00:34.600
and know what you want.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.162
What do you want in your marriage?

00:00:36.162 --> 00:00:38.322
What do you want with your
son and your daughter?

00:00:38.322 --> 00:00:39.762
What do you want in your health?

00:00:39.762 --> 00:00:41.333
What do you want financially?

00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:43.729
How much money do you want to make a year?

00:00:43.729 --> 00:00:44.993
What do you want to drive?

00:00:44.993 --> 00:00:46.212
How do you want to live?

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.232
Stop just wakin' up like a accident.

00:00:48.232 --> 00:00:50.235
What do you want?

00:00:50.235 --> 00:00:52.227
And then once you find out what you want

00:00:52.227 --> 00:00:55.174
spend the rest of your
natural life wakin' up

00:00:55.174 --> 00:00:56.818
and goin' after it.

00:00:56.818 --> 00:00:58.883
The reason why I speak
with so much passion ...

00:00:58.883 --> 00:01:02.047
E.T., why do you speak
with so much authority?

00:01:02.047 --> 00:01:04.337
'Cause I'm talkin' about my life.

00:01:04.337 --> 00:01:05.601
Not something that I read.

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:07.518
I ate out of trash cans.

00:01:08.756 --> 00:01:11.422
I had no business eatin'
out of trash cans.

00:01:11.422 --> 00:01:13.039
I lived in abandoned buildings.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:16.540
I had no business livin'
in abandoned buildings.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:18.764
But, E.T., your daddy wasn't in your life,

00:01:18.764 --> 00:01:20.461
your mom was a teenage mother.

00:01:20.461 --> 00:01:21.483
You grew up,

00:01:21.483 --> 00:01:22.493
come on E.,

00:01:22.493 --> 00:01:24.159
look at your circ, that's not an excuse.

00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:25.880
There is no excuse for not livin' up

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.296
to your fullest potential.

00:01:27.296 --> 00:01:28.576
No excuse.

00:01:28.576 --> 00:01:30.059
Worked on my gift.

00:01:30.059 --> 00:01:33.751
I realize that all of
us are born with a gift,

00:01:33.751 --> 00:01:35.080
but you've got to hone it.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.432
You know, you're not going to become great

00:01:37.432 --> 00:01:39.907
and we talk about the school of greatness.

00:01:39.907 --> 00:01:43.991
We talk about greatness
is upon you and I realized

00:01:43.991 --> 00:01:46.933
that my gift wasn't
goin' to create itself.

00:01:46.933 --> 00:01:49.165
My gift wasn't goin' to nurture itself.

00:01:49.165 --> 00:01:51.494
My gift wasn't goin' to perfect itself.

00:01:51.494 --> 00:01:54.267
That was somethin' I had to do, and so ...

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:56.742
Man before you know it we
did a video that went viral.

00:01:56.742 --> 00:01:58.945
I think it's got over 50 million hits now

00:01:58.945 --> 00:02:01.406
and we turn our passion into our profit.

00:02:01.406 --> 00:02:04.027
- Love it man, love it.

00:02:04.027 --> 00:02:05.808
- Yeah, we turn our passion into profit.

00:02:05.808 --> 00:02:07.127
You know what's so funny?

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:09.822
We want people to make guarantees to us

00:02:09.822 --> 00:02:14.647
but we not willin' to make
guarantees to ourself.

00:02:14.647 --> 00:02:17.296
Now (mumbles) like you,
somebody gave you a guarantee,

00:02:17.296 --> 00:02:19.082
30 day guarantee.

00:02:19.082 --> 00:02:20.567
In 30 days, if you don't make

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:23.219
what they told you, you was going to make,

00:02:23.219 --> 00:02:25.488
in 30 days you got an attitude,
you want your money back.

00:02:25.488 --> 00:02:28.145
But you never demanded your
money back from yourself.

00:02:28.145 --> 00:02:29.607
You've never looked at
yourself in the mirror

00:02:29.607 --> 00:02:31.476
and said you let you down.

00:02:31.476 --> 00:02:34.926
Until you get to that
point, you let you down.

00:02:34.926 --> 00:02:36.458
You never, you're not brave enough.

00:02:36.458 --> 00:02:38.036
You want to put it on somebody else.

00:02:38.036 --> 00:02:40.733
The reason why I'm not
successful is because of my boss.

00:02:40.733 --> 00:02:42.483
Have you ever looked at
yourself in the mirror

00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:44.625
and said, "I'm not gettin' up on time.

00:02:44.625 --> 00:02:46.474
"I'm not goin' to work on time.

00:02:46.474 --> 00:02:49.080
"I'm not putting' in
120% when I'm at work.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:50.450
"I let me down."

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.027
And when you get to the
point where you can say

00:02:52.027 --> 00:02:54.957
you let you down, listen
to me, no disrespect,

00:02:54.957 --> 00:02:58.122
I don't care about Glen,
that's not why I do what I do.

00:02:58.122 --> 00:02:59.247
And I love Glen.

00:02:59.247 --> 00:03:00.782
I don't come here and do what I do

00:03:00.782 --> 00:03:03.944
so Glen can affirm me, so he
can give me a pat on my back.

00:03:03.944 --> 00:03:07.766
I care more about me than I
care what Glen thinks about me.

00:03:07.766 --> 00:03:09.115
I have standards.

00:03:09.115 --> 00:03:10.404
I have values.

00:03:10.404 --> 00:03:11.645
I don't care how much you pay me,

00:03:11.645 --> 00:03:13.990
if I speak at an elementary
school for $300 dollars,

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:16.311
I chose to do that for $300 dollars.

00:03:16.311 --> 00:03:18.273
If I chose to speak at a prison for free,

00:03:18.273 --> 00:03:19.637
I chose to do that.

00:03:19.637 --> 00:03:22.231
And I will not go in there
and give those prisoners less

00:03:22.231 --> 00:03:23.972
than what somebody pays me $100,000.

00:03:23.972 --> 00:03:24.805
Why?

00:03:24.805 --> 00:03:29.672
Because I value myself enough
to give 120% or don't do it.

00:03:29.672 --> 00:03:31.311
That's the problem with some of you.

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:33.027
You always want to blame other people.

00:03:33.027 --> 00:03:35.661
You want to hold other people to the fire

00:03:35.661 --> 00:03:37.445
but you not holding yourself to the fire.

00:03:37.445 --> 00:03:39.348
You just said you givin' 50%.

00:03:39.348 --> 00:03:41.241
You owe you an explanation.

00:03:41.241 --> 00:03:42.828
You owe you an explanation.

00:03:42.828 --> 00:03:44.526
You need to look at yourself in the mirror

00:03:44.526 --> 00:03:46.830
and say why are you only giving 50%,

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.594
what's wrong with you?

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:51.058
You need to put yourself on punishment.

00:03:51.058 --> 00:03:53.862
You need to tell you, no
more TV, no more snacks,

00:03:53.862 --> 00:03:56.808
no more desserts, no more,
no, we workin' out now.

00:03:56.808 --> 00:03:58.982
No more alcohol, not right now.

00:03:58.982 --> 00:04:00.548
No, I can't handle it right now.

00:04:00.548 --> 00:04:03.832
You need to tell you that
you owe you something.

00:04:03.832 --> 00:04:06.887
You keep going to the
mall with the receipt,

00:04:06.887 --> 00:04:08.447
this isn't what you all said it was.

00:04:08.447 --> 00:04:10.519
Glen, you didn't do what you
said you was going to do.

00:04:10.519 --> 00:04:12.297
Well, you didn't do what
you were supposed to do

00:04:12.297 --> 00:04:15.606
so how am I going to do what
I'm supposed to do for you?

00:04:15.606 --> 00:04:17.159
You walk out of this
room, you owe yourself.

00:04:17.159 --> 00:04:19.582
I didn't get here makin' excuses.

00:04:19.582 --> 00:04:21.240
So what my father wasn't in my life,

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:24.129
the truth of the matter is he
ain't never come into my life.

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:25.454
So what, I'm a wait
for the rest of my life

00:04:25.454 --> 00:04:26.730
for my man to come?

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:27.833
He ain't comin'.

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:28.684
I live in America.

00:04:28.684 --> 00:04:29.923
I'm an African-American male.

00:04:29.923 --> 00:04:31.395
They don't treat us the same.

00:04:31.395 --> 00:04:32.425
There's somethin' called racism.

00:04:32.425 --> 00:04:34.120
I ain't going to cry about it.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.474
There's probably going to
be racism til the day I die

00:04:36.474 --> 00:04:38.019
but I'm not going to cry about it.

00:04:38.019 --> 00:04:39.550
I'm still going to be a millionaire.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:41.508
I'm still going to be one of
the top motivational speakers

00:04:41.508 --> 00:04:43.099
in the world.

00:04:43.099 --> 00:04:45.002
No I didn't grow up on
that side of the town,

00:04:45.002 --> 00:04:46.549
no my mama don't have no network,

00:04:46.549 --> 00:04:48.186
no I don't know a whole lot of people,

00:04:48.186 --> 00:04:50.116
no I'm not at a country club,

00:04:50.116 --> 00:04:52.125
no I don't play golf and
I don't plan on playing

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:53.740
no time soon.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:55.185
But I'm still going to be successful.

00:04:55.185 --> 00:04:56.698
I'm still going to get to where they are.

00:04:56.698 --> 00:04:57.628
Why?

00:04:57.628 --> 00:05:02.185
'Cause I owe it to myself and
can't nobody stop me but me.

00:05:02.185 --> 00:05:03.427
And you need to get rid of them excuses

00:05:03.427 --> 00:05:05.767
and you need to stop
pointing fingers at people.

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:07.361
And you need to start
pointing fingers at yourself.

00:05:07.361 --> 00:05:08.793
What did you not do?

00:05:08.793 --> 00:05:10.616
A guy asked me about two months ago,

00:05:10.616 --> 00:05:12.882
he said, "E.T., if there's
one mistake you made,

00:05:12.882 --> 00:05:14.078
"what's that one mistake you made?"

00:05:14.078 --> 00:05:15.279
I said, "I'm going to be honest with you.

00:05:15.279 --> 00:05:19.279
"My values are not in
alignment with my dreams."

00:05:22.495 --> 00:05:24.623
I said, "I want to tell you a story."

00:05:24.623 --> 00:05:25.456
I got a good friend of
mine, good friend of mine.

00:05:25.456 --> 00:05:28.347
He came to me, said, "Eric,
my marriage is not where

00:05:28.347 --> 00:05:29.606
"my marriage needs to be.

00:05:29.606 --> 00:05:30.439
"I need to make some adjustments.

00:05:30.439 --> 00:05:32.534
"I see you and your
wife, I see how much time

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:33.857
"you spend with your wife,

00:05:33.857 --> 00:05:34.690
"how much time you spend
with your children,

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:36.107
"and I want that.

00:05:37.257 --> 00:05:38.728
"You buy your wife roses regularly,

00:05:38.728 --> 00:05:40.087
"you always taking her out to eat.

00:05:40.087 --> 00:05:42.201
"I'm watchin' you, you spoil her.

00:05:42.201 --> 00:05:44.823
"E.T., what can I do?"

00:05:44.823 --> 00:05:46.060
And so I told him what to do

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.264
and guess what he started doing, God?

00:05:47.264 --> 00:05:50.056
He started doing the exact
same thing I started doing.

00:05:50.056 --> 00:05:52.397
And he said, "Eric, it's not workin'.

00:05:52.397 --> 00:05:54.379
"I'm doing exactly what you're
doin' but it's not workin'."

00:05:54.379 --> 00:05:55.212
He said, "Why isn't it workin?"

00:05:55.212 --> 00:05:56.045
I said, "You know why it's not workin'?

00:05:56.045 --> 00:05:58.735
"Because your values and your dreams,

00:05:58.735 --> 00:06:02.547
"you say you want a better marriage,

00:06:02.547 --> 00:06:04.345
"but I told you, you need to
iron your wife's clothes."

00:06:04.345 --> 00:06:05.562
You know what he told me?

00:06:05.562 --> 00:06:07.004
After while he said, "I'm going
to be honest with you Eric.

00:06:07.004 --> 00:06:08.826
"I know, you told me to
iron, you told me to wash,

00:06:08.826 --> 00:06:09.804
"you told me to cook.

00:06:09.804 --> 00:06:11.446
"But where I come from," he said,
"I'm going to be honest Eric.

00:06:11.446 --> 00:06:13.232
"When I do that, I feel like a punk."

00:06:13.232 --> 00:06:15.107
And I said, "That's why you
havin' a hard time doin' it.

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:18.108
"Because your value system
says a man is not supposed

00:06:18.108 --> 00:06:20.457
"to iron, a man is not supposed to cook,

00:06:20.457 --> 00:06:22.181
"a man is not supposed to wash dishes.

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:24.036
"That's what your value
system says, so you're doing

00:06:24.036 --> 00:06:26.735
"one thing but you're going
against your own value system.

00:06:26.735 --> 00:06:28.851
"The reason why I'm
havin' such an easy time

00:06:28.851 --> 00:06:31.364
"washin' clothes and cookin' and ironing,

00:06:31.364 --> 00:06:32.547
"you know why?

00:06:32.547 --> 00:06:34.972
"Because nothing is as
important to me as my marriage

00:06:34.972 --> 00:06:37.871
"and I'd rather be happy,
I would rather be happy

00:06:37.871 --> 00:06:39.201
"than to say I ain't no punk."

00:06:39.201 --> 00:06:42.034
Make me a punk, I want to be a punk.

00:06:42.977 --> 00:06:43.902
A happy punk.

00:06:43.902 --> 00:06:46.902
(audience applause)

00:06:47.891 --> 00:06:49.993
For real, no, a friend of
mine, he came to my house

00:06:49.993 --> 00:06:52.236
and I didn't have a mop,
and so I was on the ground,

00:06:52.236 --> 00:06:53.966
and I was moppin' the floor with a towel.

00:06:53.966 --> 00:06:55.707
And he said, "E.T., the hip-hop
preacher, you on the ground

00:06:55.707 --> 00:06:56.910
"and you moppin?"

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:57.743
I said, "Yeah."

00:06:57.743 --> 00:06:59.200
He says, "Your wife got you whipped."

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.257
I say, "You didn't know?

00:07:01.257 --> 00:07:03.859
"You just found it out?"

00:07:03.859 --> 00:07:04.995
(audience laughs)

00:07:04.995 --> 00:07:06.377
Been doing a terrible job.

00:07:06.377 --> 00:07:07.766
I'm sorry, I am whipped.

00:07:07.766 --> 00:07:09.309
And after 23 years you
should be, and if you're not,

00:07:09.309 --> 00:07:10.559
it's a problem.

00:07:11.644 --> 00:07:13.175
So listen to me, those of you that said

00:07:13.175 --> 00:07:15.075
I want to be a millionaire,
I want to be the best

00:07:15.075 --> 00:07:16.287
at this company, right?

00:07:16.287 --> 00:07:18.980
But your value system
says you believe in sleep

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:20.866
more than you believe in grinding.

00:07:20.866 --> 00:07:23.520
Your value system says you are a consumer

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:25.103
and not a producer.

00:07:25.981 --> 00:07:27.895
And you're spending more
money than you're making.

00:07:27.895 --> 00:07:28.728
Why?

00:07:28.728 --> 00:07:30.677
Because you're a consumer but
you're reading all the books

00:07:30.677 --> 00:07:32.515
and you're saying everything
the books are saying,

00:07:32.515 --> 00:07:35.445
but those books are not in
alignment with your values.

00:07:35.445 --> 00:07:37.133
If you're going to go to the next level,

00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:39.283
your values are going to have to change.

00:07:39.283 --> 00:07:42.523
I think what people get
confused is, you know,

00:07:42.523 --> 00:07:44.086
they're grinding with a goal.

00:07:44.086 --> 00:07:46.188
And I'm not saying you
shouldn't have goals.

00:07:46.188 --> 00:07:48.400
But you should be grinding
for grinding's sake.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.395
You should grind because
that's what you do.

00:07:50.395 --> 00:07:52.551
You're passionate about what you do,

00:07:52.551 --> 00:07:55.098
so you're wakin' up every
day with the concept

00:07:55.098 --> 00:07:58.527
of I have 24 hours and they're mine.

00:07:58.527 --> 00:08:01.190
This 24 hours belongs
to me and whatever I do

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:04.424
in this 24 hours will determine
where I'll be tomorrow

00:08:04.424 --> 00:08:05.635
and the next day, and I think

00:08:05.635 --> 00:08:07.327
that's what people need to focus on.

00:08:07.327 --> 00:08:09.756
Like get off of this, I
want to make six figures,

00:08:09.756 --> 00:08:10.706
I want to drive this car,

00:08:10.706 --> 00:08:11.897
I want to live in this house.

00:08:11.897 --> 00:08:14.344
I think what people
should be focusing on is,

00:08:14.344 --> 00:08:15.677
I have 24 hours.

00:08:16.914 --> 00:08:21.023
Like Oprah only has 24,
Bill Gates only has 24,

00:08:21.023 --> 00:08:24.219
like Warren Buffett only has 24 hours

00:08:24.219 --> 00:08:27.802
and in that 24 hour period,
I can either break my life

00:08:27.802 --> 00:08:29.511
or make my life.

00:08:29.511 --> 00:08:31.939
I'm not sayin' you shouldn't have goals.

00:08:31.939 --> 00:08:35.964
I just think that goals
for people is too high

00:08:35.964 --> 00:08:37.557
on the priority list.

00:08:37.557 --> 00:08:39.180
I think what should be
on the priority list

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:42.492
is goin' to bed, so you
can wake up the next day

00:08:42.492 --> 00:08:44.430
and you can grind it out.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:46.661
I'm just a dude that believes
you reap what you sew.

00:08:46.661 --> 00:08:50.068
So if you're grinding on
Monday, grinding on Tuesday,

00:08:50.068 --> 00:08:52.388
grinding on Wednesday, if you're grinding

00:08:52.388 --> 00:08:56.549
six, seven days a week for
a span of five or six years,

00:08:56.549 --> 00:08:58.513
somethin's got to come out of that.

00:08:58.513 --> 00:08:59.787
But if you're only grinding, you know,

00:08:59.787 --> 00:09:02.645
on Monday you fired up,
Wednesday you're back,

00:09:02.645 --> 00:09:04.758
you're sleepin' in,
Thursday you got, the hump

00:09:04.758 --> 00:09:08.467
of the world is up, like
I've heard people say,

00:09:08.467 --> 00:09:09.300
- Hump day.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:11.089
- Every day is hump day.

00:09:11.089 --> 00:09:12.492
Wednesday is hump day.

00:09:12.492 --> 00:09:14.584
Now Monday is hump day,
Tuesday is hump day,

00:09:14.584 --> 00:09:16.316
every day is hump day.

00:09:16.316 --> 00:09:19.705
I'm thinking if we would spend
more time on what's my goal,

00:09:19.705 --> 00:09:23.945
meaning what do I need
to accomplish in this day

00:09:23.945 --> 00:09:27.309
to live this lifestyle
and you go after it,

00:09:27.309 --> 00:09:30.776
then I think more people
will be successful.

00:09:30.776 --> 00:09:31.609
I just ran across a quote
the other day that says,

00:09:31.609 --> 00:09:34.359
education is the great equalizer.

00:09:36.224 --> 00:09:38.589
And I was like, oh, so
no matter where you are,

00:09:38.589 --> 00:09:41.108
if you feel like you
started at the bottom,

00:09:41.108 --> 00:09:42.610
if you feel like you started at the top,

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:44.304
but you want to preserve the top

00:09:44.304 --> 00:09:45.264
because just because you're at the top

00:09:45.264 --> 00:09:46.815
doesn't mean you're going
to be at the top forever.

00:09:46.815 --> 00:09:48.208
I mean, you look at
great football players,

00:09:48.208 --> 00:09:50.039
great football teams.

00:09:50.039 --> 00:09:53.863
You're not going to
automatically win because

00:09:53.863 --> 00:09:54.895
of your name.

00:09:54.895 --> 00:09:57.594
You have to keep
performing year after year.

00:09:57.594 --> 00:09:59.286
So if you're at the
bottom and you're like,

00:09:59.286 --> 00:10:01.433
man, I'm at the bottom Eric,
and I want to live life

00:10:01.433 --> 00:10:02.439
like everybody else.

00:10:02.439 --> 00:10:04.061
I want to fly first class.

00:10:04.061 --> 00:10:05.468
I want to see the world.

00:10:05.468 --> 00:10:07.885
I don't want any limitations.

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:12.907
Okay, so I'm using the word
reading but what I'm saying

00:10:12.907 --> 00:10:17.048
is education, being
enlightened, being informed.

00:10:17.048 --> 00:10:20.116
I had to realize for myself,
being a high school dropout.

00:10:20.116 --> 00:10:22.059
You can't use that excuse forever.

00:10:22.059 --> 00:10:23.953
Where I was born and where I was raised,

00:10:23.953 --> 00:10:25.705
you can't use that forever.

00:10:25.705 --> 00:10:28.825
So to me, you liberate yourself Malcolm,

00:10:28.825 --> 00:10:30.136
you talked about Malcolm.

00:10:30.136 --> 00:10:32.739
Malcolm liberated himself,
and most people don't know,

00:10:32.739 --> 00:10:36.021
Malcolm was not born wearing glasses.

00:10:36.021 --> 00:10:39.713
Malcolm had 20/20 vision
but it was in prison

00:10:39.713 --> 00:10:42.388
that Malcolm learned
to take reading serious

00:10:42.388 --> 00:10:45.112
and he read with a dim light at night.

00:10:45.112 --> 00:10:48.188
That's how he eventually lost his sight.

00:10:48.188 --> 00:10:51.479
But he lost his sight
but he gained his vision.

00:10:51.479 --> 00:10:54.852
He lost his sight but he gained
his vision at that point.

00:10:54.852 --> 00:10:57.818
So I would say to young
people who are watching us,

00:10:57.818 --> 00:10:59.377
that it's not optional.

00:10:59.377 --> 00:11:01.941
The more you read, the
more liberated you are

00:11:01.941 --> 00:11:04.591
and the more you are educated.

00:11:04.591 --> 00:11:07.632
To me, the more you can experience life

00:11:07.632 --> 00:11:09.697
like the people you're
probably looking at and sayin',

00:11:09.697 --> 00:11:11.096
I wish I could live like that person.

00:11:11.096 --> 00:11:11.929
- Yeah.

00:11:11.929 --> 00:11:12.762
- What's you why?

00:11:12.762 --> 00:11:14.182
Hey, if I don't give you all nothin' else,

00:11:14.182 --> 00:11:15.764
